  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Pulmonx faces a mixed demand picture, with worldwide revenue declining year-over-year on both a reported and constant-currency basis. U.S. revenue softened, while international performance was dragged by China; excluding that market, international revenue grew solidly, suggesting underlying demand remains intact elsewhere. The company added new U.S. treating centers, indicating continued commercial expansion despite near-term headwinds. Macro and geopolitical factors, including foreign-exchange pressure, weighed on reported results, but the core procedure volume trajectory appears to be stabilizing.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership acknowledged the top-line softness while expressing confidence in a return to growth in the second half of the year, reiterating full-year guidance. Management proactively reduced operating expenses and improved gross margin, extending the cash runway without sacrificing strategic initiatives. The team continues to advance the AeriSeal clinical program and is executing on commercial productivity improvements, signaling a focus on operational discipline and long-term value creation amid a challenging revenue environment.",
